-- title:
--   Lemma 1, p.8 — MRF conditionals within $e^{\pm2\Delta}$ of the vertex law and $e^{\pm4\Delta}$ of the marginal
-- statement:
--   Let $t$ be generated by a Markov random field with alphabets $T_i$, vertex potentials $\psi_i$, local hyperedge potentials and maximum weighted degree $\Delta$. Then for every item $i$, every $t_i\in T_i$ and every $t_{-i}\in T_{-i}$:
--
--   $$
--   \frac{e^{\psi_i(t_i)}}{\sum_{t_i'\in T_i}e^{\psi_i(t_i')}}\,e^{-2\Delta}\;\le\; f_i(t_i\mid t_{-i})\;\le\;\frac{e^{\psi_i(t_i)}}{\sum_{t_i'\in T_i}e^{\psi_i(t_i')}}\,e^{2\Delta},
--   $$
--
--   and
--
--   $$
--   f_i(t_i)\,e^{-4\Delta}\;\le\; f_i(t_i\mid t_{-i})\;\le\; f_i(t_i)\,e^{4\Delta}.
--   $$
--
--   The conditional law of one item given the others is thus within a factor $e^{\pm4\Delta}$ of its marginal; this is the basic tool by which every independent-items argument of the paper is transferred to MRFs.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: item values t_i of unspecified sign (Def 1: 'interpret ti as the value of item i') → values in ℝ≥0; reason: the proofs use t_i ≥ 0 throughout (Lemma 22 drops π_i ≤ 1 against t_i, Lemma 7 uses c_i c_j ≥ 0, Theorem 2 uses C ≤ Σ t_i); item values are nonnegative in this literature
--   - reading: alphabets Σ_v / type space T of unspecified cardinality → finite alphabets (Finset), finite support; reason: Def 4 takes a max over all configurations and every sum of the paper ranges over a finite T; the duality benchmark [14] is for finite type spaces
-- source:
--   Cai & Oikonomou, On Simple Mechanisms for Dependent Items, arXiv:2106.10814v2, Lemma 1, p.8 (PDF 9)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SimpleMechMRF_TypeDist
import Definitions.Def_SimpleMechMRF_MRF

open scoped NNReal

namespace SimpleMechMRF

/-- **Lemma 1** (Cai & Oikonomou, *On Simple Mechanisms for Dependent Items*,
arXiv:2106.10814v2, p. 8, PDF 9). Let `t` be generated by an MRF `G` with law `D = G.law` and
maximum weighted degree `Δ`. For every item `i` and every `t ∈ ×ⱼ Tⱼ` (i.e. `tᵢ ∈ Tᵢ`,
`t₋ᵢ ∈ T₋ᵢ`):

* `e^{ψᵢ(tᵢ)} / Σ_{t'ᵢ∈Tᵢ} e^{ψᵢ(t'ᵢ)} · e^{−2Δ} ≤ fᵢ(tᵢ | t₋ᵢ) ≤ e^{ψᵢ(tᵢ)} / Σ_{t'ᵢ∈Tᵢ} e^{ψᵢ(t'ᵢ)} · e^{2Δ}`, and
* `fᵢ(tᵢ) · e^{−4Δ} ≤ fᵢ(tᵢ | t₋ᵢ) ≤ fᵢ(tᵢ) · e^{4Δ}`.

**Formalization Note.** Alphabets are finite sets of nonnegative reals; `fᵢ(tᵢ | t₋ᵢ)` is
`G.law.cond i t` and `fᵢ(tᵢ)` is `G.law.marg i (t i)`. -/
theorem lemma_1 {n : ℕ} (G : MRF n) (i : Fin n) (t : Fin n → ℝ≥0) (ht : t ∈ G.configs) :
    Real.exp (G.ψv i (t i)) / (∑ s ∈ G.A i, Real.exp (G.ψv i s)) *
        Real.exp (-2 * G.maxWeightedDegree) ≤ G.law.cond i t ∧
    G.law.cond i t ≤ Real.exp (G.ψv i (t i)) / (∑ s ∈ G.A i, Real.exp (G.ψv i s)) *
        Real.exp (2 * G.maxWeightedDegree) ∧
    G.law.marg i (t i) * Real.exp (-4 * G.maxWeightedDegree) ≤ G.law.cond i t ∧
    G.law.cond i t ≤ G.law.marg i (t i) * Real.exp (4 * G.maxWeightedDegree) := by sorry

end SimpleMechMRF
